<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wide Is My Motherland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Широка страна моя родная, Shiroka strana moya rodnaya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Wide Is My Motherland&quot;, also called the &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> of the Motherland&quot;, is a Soviet patriotic song of 1936 with music by Isaac Dunaevsky and words by Vasily Lebedev-Kumach. They wrote it for the film Circus, working on it for half a year and changing tune and words again and again; the version they settled on was their thirty-sixth.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Wide Is My Motherland</b>&quot;, also called the &quot;Song of the Motherland&quot;, is a Soviet patriotic song of 1936 with music by Isaac Dunaevsky and words by Vasily Lebedev-Kumach.</blockquote><a href="/songs/wide-is-my-motherland">Wide Is My Motherland</a></li></ul></section>
